[[:db/retract 17592186148937 :answer-field/choices 17592186148938] [:db/retract 17592186148937 :answer-field/choices 17592186148939] [:db/retract 17592186148937 :answer-field/choices 17592186148940] [:db/retract 17592186148937 :answer-field/choices 17592186148941] [:db/retract 17592186148937 :answer-field/choices 17592186148942] [:db/retract 17592186148943 :answer-field/choices 17592186148944] [:db/retract 17592186148943 :answer-field/choices 17592186148945] [:db/retract 17592186148943 :answer-field/choices 17592186148946] [:db/retract 17592186148943 :answer-field/choices 17592186148947] [:db/retract 17592186148943 :answer-field/choices 17592186148948] {:db/id 17592186152284 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d99b4ca2-1051-5b19-b0ca-e022766a3c13" "question-cbabadfa-0d4d-5a45-80b7-bf364847e945" "question-fe7e11df-3bda-53fa-998a-37d8783a4f32"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151994 :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(1)=e$ into our general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e & =A{e}^{1}+B{e}^{-2(1)} \\\\ e & =Ae+B{e}^{-2} \\\\ A & =1-B{e}^{-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition $y'(1) = e^{-2},$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\ny' = Ae^x - 2Be^{-x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y'(1)=e^{-2}$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2} & =A{e}^{1}-2B{e}^{-2(1)} \\\\ {e}^{-2} & =Ae-2B{e}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}A=1-B{e}^{-3} \\\\ {e}^{-2}=Ae-2B{e}^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A = 1 - B e ^{-3}$ in the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2} & =(1-B{e}^{-3})e-2B{e}^{-2} \\\\ 1 & ={e}^{3}-B-2B \\\\ B & =\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting $B= \\dfrac {e ^ 3 - 1} 3$ back into the equation $A = 1-Be^{-3}$ gives\n\n$$\nA = 1 -  \\dfrac {(e ^ 3 - 1) e ^ {-3}} 3 =   \\dfrac {2 +  e ^ {-3}} 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution of the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny =  \\dfrac {  e ^ {-3} + 2} 3  e^{x} + \\dfrac {e ^ 3 - 1} 3 e^{-2x}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152285 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-385b9591-ad6c-5296-82bc-53313648dde5" "question-4a808d33-3853-58bc-a004-7d852404000e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151995 :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have a repeated root $\\lambda = 2,$ so we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\ny = A e ^ { 2 x} + B x e ^ {2 x}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=3$ into our general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =A{e}^{2(0)}+B(0){e}^{2(0)} \\\\ 3 & =A{e}^{0}+0 \\\\ 3 & =A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition $y' (0) = 2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\ny'  = 2 A e ^ {2 x} +  B e ^ { 2 x} + 2 B x e ^{ 2 x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y'(0)=2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =2A{e}^{2(0)}+B{e}^{2(0)}+2B(0){e}^{2(0)} \\\\ 2 & =2A{e}^{0}+B{e}^{0}+0 \\\\ 2 & =2A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3=A \\\\ 2=2A+B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=3$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =6+B \\\\ B & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=3$ and $B=-4,$ and therefore the solution is \n\n$$\ny = 3 e ^ { 2 x } - 4 x e ^ { 2 x}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152286 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e50b91c5-e53d-5ab3-9544-957263ee499e" "question-00d6379f-1cac-59b7-a19a-344de30af15c" "question-b8669bf2-0ec8-592b-af07-c83c24aa14e8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152287 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ad9f0a12-4237-5c82-9aa7-6fbbeb604773" "question-1a78761c-d0ad-5651-b02a-e973e2385ada" "question-4d183a38-3bd7-5a3d-b0c0-6bbf656b9b64"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152401 :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-2y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-2{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -2)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-1$ or $\\lambda =2.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nNow let us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=1.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-4.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-A{e}^{-x}+2B{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-A+2B=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B=1 \\\\ -A+2B=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=2,B=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2{e}^{-x}-{e}^{2x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186148937 :answer-field/correct "answer-ed6783de-fb3d-5d54-8286-c1aa1c50555e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f1cb52c6-ae5e-5d19-9335-21304dab5d85" "answer-ed6783de-fb3d-5d54-8286-c1aa1c50555e" "answer-b8613441-e69b-5939-ae74-8cc30a7bd06d" "answer-6e031bec-4024-5bff-a0a7-6c68243bedda" "answer-a8b5524f-6144-5f88-9a69-8e05643972e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1cb52c6-ae5e-5d19-9335-21304dab5d85" :answer/id #uuid "f1cb52c6-ae5e-5d19-9335-21304dab5d85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x}+2{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed6783de-fb3d-5d54-8286-c1aa1c50555e" :answer/id #uuid "ed6783de-fb3d-5d54-8286-c1aa1c50555e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-x}-{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8613441-e69b-5939-ae74-8cc30a7bd06d" :answer/id #uuid "b8613441-e69b-5939-ae74-8cc30a7bd06d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4{e}^{-x}-3{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e031bec-4024-5bff-a0a7-6c68243bedda" :answer/id #uuid "6e031bec-4024-5bff-a0a7-6c68243bedda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8b5524f-6144-5f88-9a69-8e05643972e0" :answer/id #uuid "a8b5524f-6144-5f88-9a69-8e05643972e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d99b4ca2-1051-5b19-b0ca-e022766a3c13" :question/id #uuid "d99b4ca2-1051-5b19-b0ca-e022766a3c13" :question/math-academy-id "q-130340" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-7{y}^{′}-8y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{8x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-7{y}^{′}-8y=0,\\,y(0)=0,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(0)=-18.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=0.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-18,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-A{e}^{-x}+8B{e}^{8x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-18$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-A+8B=-18.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B=0 \\\\ 8B-A=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=2,B=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2{e}^{-x}-2{e}^{8x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7b57be19-b31a-5529-8b7d-a45f836917f3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7b57be19-b31a-5529-8b7d-a45f836917f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b57be19-b31a-5529-8b7d-a45f836917f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1029e982-1cb8-59a1-800a-6eddc8bb0c8a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4e18fb50-aa99-53db-bb7e-d22c8a9849c1" "answer-1029e982-1cb8-59a1-800a-6eddc8bb0c8a" "answer-204931ce-cb59-5974-b135-26060d7cd2da" "answer-0d40d78b-f10f-551a-bf45-f2b3a9619d8b" "answer-8d32c42c-4dc2-5fb7-b932-58cc4bb05b0d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e18fb50-aa99-53db-bb7e-d22c8a9849c1" :answer/id #uuid "4e18fb50-aa99-53db-bb7e-d22c8a9849c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-x}+2{e}^{8x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1029e982-1cb8-59a1-800a-6eddc8bb0c8a" :answer/id #uuid "1029e982-1cb8-59a1-800a-6eddc8bb0c8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-x}-2{e}^{8x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-204931ce-cb59-5974-b135-26060d7cd2da" :answer/id #uuid "204931ce-cb59-5974-b135-26060d7cd2da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3{e}^{-x}-3{e}^{8x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d40d78b-f10f-551a-bf45-f2b3a9619d8b" :answer/id #uuid "0d40d78b-f10f-551a-bf45-f2b3a9619d8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}-{e}^{8x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d32c42c-4dc2-5fb7-b932-58cc4bb05b0d" :answer/id #uuid "8d32c42c-4dc2-5fb7-b932-58cc4bb05b0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{8x}-{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cbabadfa-0d4d-5a45-80b7-bf364847e945" :question/id #uuid "cbabadfa-0d4d-5a45-80b7-bf364847e945" :question/math-academy-id "q-130339" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-9y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{3x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-9y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A{e}^{-3x}+3B{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-3A+3B=0.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B=2 \\\\ -3A+3B=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=1,B=1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-3x}+{e}^{3x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-65f2e16b-2b82-5cc9-a8ad-cf8d984e234d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-65f2e16b-2b82-5cc9-a8ad-cf8d984e234d" :answer-field/id #uuid "65f2e16b-2b82-5cc9-a8ad-cf8d984e234d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ef9a2e7c-4ae2-58e1-bf2d-a13b03f1e88d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-596a6ddd-3d0f-5678-9be7-860b0f40740a" "answer-ebfe6c00-24b3-5751-94bf-30b104f0e51e" "answer-419e161a-490d-5c6f-a7e4-eaa1b01c0887" "answer-9d1aafac-6504-5529-8eb6-e512b18e650b" "answer-ef9a2e7c-4ae2-58e1-bf2d-a13b03f1e88d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-596a6ddd-3d0f-5678-9be7-860b0f40740a" :answer/id #uuid "596a6ddd-3d0f-5678-9be7-860b0f40740a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-3x}+3{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebfe6c00-24b3-5751-94bf-30b104f0e51e" :answer/id #uuid "ebfe6c00-24b3-5751-94bf-30b104f0e51e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-419e161a-490d-5c6f-a7e4-eaa1b01c0887" :answer/id #uuid "419e161a-490d-5c6f-a7e4-eaa1b01c0887" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d1aafac-6504-5529-8eb6-e512b18e650b" :answer/id #uuid "9d1aafac-6504-5529-8eb6-e512b18e650b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=5{e}^{-3x}-3{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef9a2e7c-4ae2-58e1-bf2d-a13b03f1e88d" :answer/id #uuid "ef9a2e7c-4ae2-58e1-bf2d-a13b03f1e88d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-3x}+{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fe7e11df-3bda-53fa-998a-37d8783a4f32" :question/id #uuid "fe7e11df-3bda-53fa-998a-37d8783a4f32" :question/math-academy-id "q-7789" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-5y=0,\\,y(1)=1,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(1)=7.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda -5 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +5)(\\lambda -1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =-5,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow we find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(1)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA{e}^{-5}+Be=1.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=7,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-5A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(1)=7$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-5A{e}^{-5}+Be=7.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-5}+Be=1 \\\\ -5A{e}^{-5}+Be=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=-{e}^{5},B=2{e}^{-1}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{e}^{5}\\cdot {e}^{-5x}+2{e}^{-1}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-5x+5}+2{e}^{x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-028dd5c8-1b67-5564-af86-02df34d419e6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-028dd5c8-1b67-5564-af86-02df34d419e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "028dd5c8-1b67-5564-af86-02df34d419e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7569b8e5-0cd2-5f8b-acf3-e84018c38232" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bc750cc4-f587-579a-b2ff-04773b6d8134" "answer-ec87e771-a6a7-53b3-8bba-b2c753c87011" "answer-26037b2c-fdab-548c-ba39-81bdf3515e82" "answer-7569b8e5-0cd2-5f8b-acf3-e84018c38232" "answer-d405ca87-259a-5550-ad19-3cb0d9609b6d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc750cc4-f587-579a-b2ff-04773b6d8134" :answer/id #uuid "bc750cc4-f587-579a-b2ff-04773b6d8134" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-5x+5}+3{e}^{x-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec87e771-a6a7-53b3-8bba-b2c753c87011" :answer/id #uuid "ec87e771-a6a7-53b3-8bba-b2c753c87011" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-7{e}^{-5x+5}+8{e}^{x-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26037b2c-fdab-548c-ba39-81bdf3515e82" :answer/id #uuid "26037b2c-fdab-548c-ba39-81bdf3515e82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-3x}+2{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7569b8e5-0cd2-5f8b-acf3-e84018c38232" :answer/id #uuid "7569b8e5-0cd2-5f8b-acf3-e84018c38232" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-5x+5}+2{e}^{x-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d405ca87-259a-5550-ad19-3cb0d9609b6d" :answer/id #uuid "d405ca87-259a-5550-ad19-3cb0d9609b6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3{e}^{4x-4}-2{e}^{x-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152777 :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-3$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=-3.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A{e}^{-3x}-4B{e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-3A-4B=2.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B=-3 \\\\ -3A-4B=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=-10,B=7.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-10{e}^{-3x}+7{e}^{-4x}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-385b9591-ad6c-5296-82bc-53313648dde5" :question/id #uuid "385b9591-ad6c-5296-82bc-53313648dde5" :question/math-academy-id "q-7797" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+4y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=3.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+4\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+4{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +2) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =-2$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+Bx{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=1.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=3.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-2A{e}^{-2x}+-2Bx{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=3$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-2A+B=3.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=1$ gives $B=5.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-2x}+5x{e}^{-2x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c771707c-db14-54e5-9719-2f5b8eb0740c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c771707c-db14-54e5-9719-2f5b8eb0740c" :answer-field/id #uuid "c771707c-db14-54e5-9719-2f5b8eb0740c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1f869bf6-107f-5db7-b5a5-33d521155f66" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0137ee6e-c523-5606-ab61-bd96f6cd46e6" "answer-1f869bf6-107f-5db7-b5a5-33d521155f66" "answer-462f6db9-3bd4-53ff-a35f-8656edd69646" "answer-42d8c8b0-9be5-591b-b0ec-8b768f062a61" "answer-6bd8cda8-05fa-59b2-9091-e867beec2408"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0137ee6e-c523-5606-ab61-bd96f6cd46e6" :answer/id #uuid "0137ee6e-c523-5606-ab61-bd96f6cd46e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}+2x{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f869bf6-107f-5db7-b5a5-33d521155f66" :answer/id #uuid "1f869bf6-107f-5db7-b5a5-33d521155f66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}+5x{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-462f6db9-3bd4-53ff-a35f-8656edd69646" :answer/id #uuid "462f6db9-3bd4-53ff-a35f-8656edd69646" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}+x{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42d8c8b0-9be5-591b-b0ec-8b768f062a61" :answer/id #uuid "42d8c8b0-9be5-591b-b0ec-8b768f062a61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}+x{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bd8cda8-05fa-59b2-9091-e867beec2408" :answer/id #uuid "6bd8cda8-05fa-59b2-9091-e867beec2408" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}-5x{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186348067 :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+3\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{9}{4}{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +\\frac{9}{4}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +\\frac{9}{4} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{2})(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{2}) & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =\\frac{3}{2}$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x/2}+Bx{e}^{-3x/2}.\n$$\n\nLet us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \nSubstituting $y(1)={e}^{-1/2}$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-3/2}+B{e}^{-3/2} & ={e}^{-1/2} \\\\ A+B & =e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-1/2}.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\frac{3}{2}A{e}^{-3/2x}+B{e}^{-3/2x}-\\frac{3}{2}Bx{e}^{-3/2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-1/2}$ into the above gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}A{e}^{-3/2}-\\frac{1}{2}B{e}^{-3/2} & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-1/2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}A-\\frac{1}{2}B & =\\frac{1}{2}e \\\\ -3A-B & =e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B=e \\\\ -3A-B=e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=-e,B=2e.$\n\nNow we get the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-e\\cdot {e}^{-3x/2}+2e\\cdot x{e}^{-3x/2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3x/2+1}+2x{e}^{-3x/2+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152402 :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+9y=0,\\,y(0)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +9 & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda +3)}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have a repeated root $\\lambda =-3,$ so we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+Bx{e}^{-3x}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=-2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{-3x}-3Bx{e}^{-3x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-3A+B=2.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=-2$ gives $B=-4.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-2{e}^{-3x}-4x{e}^{-3x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186148943 :answer-field/correct "answer-0922b0c1-b8d5-5acc-824f-3d66df13cd2c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7aec91b-5023-511f-94e5-52c5a358d29c" "answer-0922b0c1-b8d5-5acc-824f-3d66df13cd2c" "answer-0843ecfa-4e3a-592f-95c8-ebdbd00c572f" "answer-3dbb7a89-524b-5fb7-8987-365ee58f1aac" "answer-af81ca3e-eea1-5fa8-b729-88ef645ad2ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7aec91b-5023-511f-94e5-52c5a358d29c" :answer/id #uuid "f7aec91b-5023-511f-94e5-52c5a358d29c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-3x}+8x{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0922b0c1-b8d5-5acc-824f-3d66df13cd2c" :answer/id #uuid "0922b0c1-b8d5-5acc-824f-3d66df13cd2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-3x}-4x{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0843ecfa-4e3a-592f-95c8-ebdbd00c572f" :answer/id #uuid "0843ecfa-4e3a-592f-95c8-ebdbd00c572f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-3x}-x{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3dbb7a89-524b-5fb7-8987-365ee58f1aac" :answer/id #uuid "3dbb7a89-524b-5fb7-8987-365ee58f1aac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{3x}+2x{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af81ca3e-eea1-5fa8-b729-88ef645ad2ee" :answer/id #uuid "af81ca3e-eea1-5fa8-b729-88ef645ad2ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{3x}-x{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4a808d33-3853-58bc-a004-7d852404000e" :question/id #uuid "4a808d33-3853-58bc-a004-7d852404000e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130347" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+14{y}^{′}+49y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-7x}+Bx{e}^{-7x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+14{y}^{′}+49y=0,\\,y(0)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=8.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=-1.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=8,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-7A{e}^{-7x}+B{e}^{-7x}-7Bx{e}^{-7x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=8$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-7A+B=8.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=-1$ gives $B=1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-{e}^{-7x}+x{e}^{-7x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b628b5a8-23fe-5a39-8e61-e3f1bcd259c0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b628b5a8-23fe-5a39-8e61-e3f1bcd259c0" :answer-field/id #uuid "b628b5a8-23fe-5a39-8e61-e3f1bcd259c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f7f42718-e600-5ca9-99e4-263408373f71" :answer-field/choices ["answer-090f99d5-9625-5409-8bfa-8e2c4cd59aac" "answer-f7f42718-e600-5ca9-99e4-263408373f71" "answer-203c8f4e-c8c1-5cb3-9c03-69fcae139338" "answer-da315c42-36d1-50ab-b060-34532474faac" "answer-419328d7-32fd-5588-ac38-f02df1730edf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-090f99d5-9625-5409-8bfa-8e2c4cd59aac" :answer/id #uuid "090f99d5-9625-5409-8bfa-8e2c4cd59aac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-7x}+8x{e}^{-7x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7f42718-e600-5ca9-99e4-263408373f71" :answer/id #uuid "f7f42718-e600-5ca9-99e4-263408373f71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-7x}+x{e}^{-7x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-203c8f4e-c8c1-5cb3-9c03-69fcae139338" :answer/id #uuid "203c8f4e-c8c1-5cb3-9c03-69fcae139338" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-7x}-2x{e}^{-7x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da315c42-36d1-50ab-b060-34532474faac" :answer/id #uuid "da315c42-36d1-50ab-b060-34532474faac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-7x}-7x{e}^{-7x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-419328d7-32fd-5588-ac38-f02df1730edf" :answer/id #uuid "419328d7-32fd-5588-ac38-f02df1730edf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-7x}-x{e}^{-7x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186393765 :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-8\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+16{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +16) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +16 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =4$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{4x}+Bx{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nLet us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(1)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA{e}^{4}+B{e}^{4}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=-1.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4A{e}^{4x}+B{e}^{4x}+4Bx{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n4A{e}^{4}+5B{e}^{4}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{4}+B{e}^{4}=2 \\\\ 4A{e}^{4}+5B{e}^{4}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=11{e}^{-4},B=-9{e}^{-4}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =11{e}^{-4}\\cdot {e}^{4x}-9{e}^{-4}\\cdot x{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =11{e}^{4x-4}-9x{e}^{4x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-e50b91c5-e53d-5ab3-9544-957263ee499e" :question/id #uuid "e50b91c5-e53d-5ab3-9544-957263ee499e" :question/math-academy-id "q-81397" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x),\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3y=0,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2\\sqrt{3}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=2\\sqrt{3},$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=A\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=2\\sqrt{3}$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3}=A\\sqrt{3}\\,⟹\\,A=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-408b0afd-e826-5064-a8e5-e44f09ba38cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-408b0afd-e826-5064-a8e5-e44f09ba38cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "408b0afd-e826-5064-a8e5-e44f09ba38cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7428c405-4302-51f7-bc5d-fea12e12217f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f9d3393f-9411-5f1f-a0aa-92424adb8c2b" "answer-aa31fab2-2bea-5ce6-a508-c29c038b4b72" "answer-7428c405-4302-51f7-bc5d-fea12e12217f" "answer-067e7b03-611d-5b4d-b180-2ffdccf4d076" "answer-59dfe9fd-988f-53c2-855f-b1614812537d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9d3393f-9411-5f1f-a0aa-92424adb8c2b" :answer/id #uuid "f9d3393f-9411-5f1f-a0aa-92424adb8c2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa31fab2-2bea-5ce6-a508-c29c038b4b72" :answer/id #uuid "aa31fab2-2bea-5ce6-a508-c29c038b4b72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7428c405-4302-51f7-bc5d-fea12e12217f" :answer/id #uuid "7428c405-4302-51f7-bc5d-fea12e12217f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-067e7b03-611d-5b4d-b180-2ffdccf4d076" :answer/id #uuid "067e7b03-611d-5b4d-b180-2ffdccf4d076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59dfe9fd-988f-53c2-855f-b1614812537d" :answer/id #uuid "59dfe9fd-988f-53c2-855f-b1614812537d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-00d6379f-1cac-59b7-a19a-344de30af15c" :question/id #uuid "00d6379f-1cac-59b7-a19a-344de30af15c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130351" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x),\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7y=0,\\,y(0)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=A\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)-B\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n0=A\\sqrt{7}\\,⟹\\,A=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4e73778b-1989-56f5-a344-4df7b08156a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4e73778b-1989-56f5-a344-4df7b08156a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e73778b-1989-56f5-a344-4df7b08156a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d575387f-ab5a-5abb-b0cd-aa50f48971a0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8fc56a83-a0f5-5d43-aa8f-5d18e267ba12" "answer-d575387f-ab5a-5abb-b0cd-aa50f48971a0" "answer-924b9c7c-fba8-53a4-8c7d-12b59a208e50" "answer-ae7514f0-79da-5951-b071-38c575f33ed9" "answer-c65bb0d4-b401-58a8-9321-68e4246fafaf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fc56a83-a0f5-5d43-aa8f-5d18e267ba12" :answer/id #uuid "8fc56a83-a0f5-5d43-aa8f-5d18e267ba12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d575387f-ab5a-5abb-b0cd-aa50f48971a0" :answer/id #uuid "d575387f-ab5a-5abb-b0cd-aa50f48971a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-924b9c7c-fba8-53a4-8c7d-12b59