answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e27ee5a-1f56-520e-bd93-b277256b9d3a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-454410df-f8e1-54f6-9e27-a2798142e99e" "answer-5b280312-42b5-5848-bb8a-62dfe17d7a2d" "answer-1b4c76a5-9a78-55cd-9899-c617f65dbb8f" "answer-c0ad627a-9899-5f34-94c4-32a5c8fa8625" "answer-4e27ee5a-1f56-520e-bd93-b277256b9d3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-454410df-f8e1-54f6-9e27-a2798142e99e" :answer/id #uuid "454410df-f8e1-54f6-9e27-a2798142e99e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡11x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b280312-42b5-5848-bb8a-62dfe17d7a2d" :answer/id #uuid "5b280312-42b5-5848-bb8a-62dfe17d7a2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b4c76a5-9a78-55cd-9899-c617f65dbb8f" :answer/id #uuid "1b4c76a5-9a78-55cd-9899-c617f65dbb8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=11\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0ad627a-9899-5f34-94c4-32a5c8fa8625" :answer/id #uuid "c0ad627a-9899-5f34-94c4-32a5c8fa8625" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e27ee5a-1f56-520e-bd93-b277256b9d3a" :answer/id #uuid "4e27ee5a-1f56-520e-bd93-b277256b9d3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ad9f0a12-4237-5c82-9aa7-6fbbeb604773" :question/id #uuid "ad9f0a12-4237-5c82-9aa7-6fbbeb604773" :question/math-academy-id "q-94027" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+13y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+13y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=1.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-1,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-2{e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+{e}^{-2x}(-3P\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+3Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-1$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-2P+3Q=-1.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=1$ gives $Q=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-92b560c3-a3e3-5fae-81d1-ba12be4a1dcc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-92b560c3-a3e3-5fae-81d1-ba12be4a1dcc" :answer-field/id #uuid "92b560c3-a3e3-5fae-81d1-ba12be4a1dcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-aa4bbbd3-9f33-5dfb-b89b-72bf0b2ad247" :answer-field/choices ["answer-676537c8-4285-5aad-a757-a9d82bb77416" "answer-aa4bbbd3-9f33-5dfb-b89b-72bf0b2ad247" "answer-bc331650-5409-5760-9fea-61f15da13246" "answer-93f7ea21-c612-5811-b154-48179ccad499" "answer-d49931e9-d307-5540-8815-ad67d0cb20b2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-676537c8-4285-5aad-a757-a9d82bb77416" :answer/id #uuid "676537c8-4285-5aad-a757-a9d82bb77416" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa4bbbd3-9f33-5dfb-b89b-72bf0b2ad247" :answer/id #uuid "aa4bbbd3-9f33-5dfb-b89b-72bf0b2ad247" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc331650-5409-5760-9fea-61f15da13246" :answer/id #uuid "bc331650-5409-5760-9fea-61f15da13246" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93f7ea21-c612-5811-b154-48179ccad499" :answer/id #uuid "93f7ea21-c612-5811-b154-48179ccad499" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d49931e9-d307-5540-8815-ad67d0cb20b2" :answer/id #uuid "d49931e9-d307-5540-8815-ad67d0cb20b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1a78761c-d0ad-5651-b02a-e973e2385ada" :question/id #uuid "1a78761c-d0ad-5651-b02a-e973e2385ada" :question/math-academy-id "q-7893" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+10y=0,\\,y(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=1,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+10{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +10) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +10=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +10 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1)^{2}-1+10 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2} & =-9 \\\\ \\lambda +1 & =\\pm 3\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-1\\pm 3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants $P$ and $Q.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q{e}^{-\\pi /6} & =1 \\\\ Q & ={e}^{\\pi /6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-{e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+{e}^{-x}(-3P\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+3Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-Q{e}^{-\\pi /6}-3P{e}^{-\\pi /6} & =2 \\\\ -Q-3P & =2{e}^{\\pi /6} \\\\ -{e}^{\\pi /6}-3P & =2{e}^{\\pi /6} \\\\ P & =-{e}^{\\pi /6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $Q={e}^{\\pi /6}$ and $P=-{e}^{\\pi /6}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-x}(-{e}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+{e}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x) \\\\  & ={e}^{-x+\\pi /6}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c4eeea1c-8cea-5fa0-af41-255c4c40e45b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c4eeea1c-8cea-5fa0-af41-255c4c40e45b" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4eeea1c-8cea-5fa0-af41-255c4c40e45b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-50868c33-8407-589c-bfad-291f32fb6f3e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bf0206d8-67a6-5880-99ad-0ae8bdd971eb" "answer-bfb9cf92-1a16-58f2-9b54-96a4a29652b7" "answer-50868c33-8407-589c-bfad-291f32fb6f3e" "answer-9fa32848-af4f-5ffd-ad94-45426b415ba6" "answer-2b282211-1d23-5349-b3f7-ddda48199c41"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf0206d8-67a6-5880-99ad-0ae8bdd971eb" :answer/id #uuid "bf0206d8-67a6-5880-99ad-0ae8bdd971eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x+\\pi /6}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfb9cf92-1a16-58f2-9b54-96a4a29652b7" :answer/id #uuid "bfb9cf92-1a16-58f2-9b54-96a4a29652b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x+\\pi /6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-50868c33-8407-589c-bfad-291f32fb6f3e" :answer/id #uuid "50868c33-8407-589c-bfad-291f32fb6f3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-x+\\pi /6}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fa32848-af4f-5ffd-ad94-45426b415ba6" :answer/id #uuid "9fa32848-af4f-5ffd-ad94-45426b415ba6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{x-\\pi /6}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b282211-1d23-5349-b3f7-ddda48199c41" :answer/id #uuid "2b282211-1d23-5349-b3f7-ddda48199c41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{x-\\pi /6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4d183a38-3bd7-5a3d-b0c0-6bbf656b9b64" :question/id #uuid "4d183a38-3bd7-5a3d-b0c0-6bbf656b9b64" :question/math-academy-id "q-130533" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+2y=0,\\,y(0)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+2{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +2=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +1)-1+2 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda -1 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =1\\pm \\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants $P$ and $Q.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=-2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=-2.\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=4.$ We differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={e}^{x}(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+{e}^{x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-2+Q=-4\\,⟹\\,Q=-2.\n$$\n\nSo we have $P=-2$ and $Q=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aab4196f-6b76-5bce-9655-3bb0e187a2a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aab4196f-6b76-5bce-9655-3bb0e187a2a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "aab4196f-6b76-5bce-9655-3bb0e187a2a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-697fcea0-b422-5fd9-8a3c-b4de3653327a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c906702c-bb29-5e13-834a-3f940496c811" "answer-0db04b57-7e0b-51b5-9068-627b530d93d5" "answer-697fcea0-b422-5fd9-8a3c-b4de3653327a" "answer-a8ec0f9e-bd19-5a45-8045-94296328023e" "answer-c75b25a4-08bf-5b34-b13b-1d43f8125742"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c906702c-bb29-5e13-834a-3f940496c811" :answer/id #uuid "c906702c-bb29-5e13-834a-3f940496c811" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0db04b57-7e0b-51b5-9068-627b530d93d5" :answer/id #uuid "0db04b57-7e0b-51b5-9068-627b530d93d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-697fcea0-b422-5fd9-8a3c-b4de3653327a" :answer/id #uuid "697fcea0-b422-5fd9-8a3c-b4de3653327a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8ec0f9e-bd19-5a45-8045-94296328023e" :answer/id #uuid "a8ec0f9e-bd19-5a45-8045-94296328023e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c75b25a4-08bf-5b34-b13b-1d43f8125742" :answer/id #uuid "c75b25a4-08bf-5b34-b13b-1d43f8125742" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153337 :tutorial/content "Let's find the particular solution for the **initial value problem**:\n\n$$\ny'' + 5y' + 6y =0, \\ \\ y(0) = 1, \\ \\ y' (0) = 1.\n$$\n\nWe start with the general solution:\n\n$$\ny(x) = Ae^{-2x} + Be^{-3x}.\n$$\n\n**Step 1: Apply the first initial condition, $y(0)=1.$**\nSubstituting $x=0$ and $y=1$ into the general solution gives our first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =A{e}^{-2(0)}+B{e}^{-3(0)} \\\\ 1 & =A{e}^{0}+B{e}^{0} \\\\ 1 & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2: Apply the second initial condition, $y'(0)=1.$**\nFirst, we need to find the derivative, $y'(x){:}$\n\n$$\ny'(x) =  -2 A e ^ { -2 x}  -3 B e ^ {-3 x}.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $x=0$ and $y'=1$ gives our second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-2A{e}^{-2(0)}-3B{e}^{-3(0)} \\\\ 1 & =-2A{e}^{0}-3B{e}^{0} \\\\ 1 & =-2A-3B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3: Solve the system of equations for $A$ and $B.$**\nWe have a system of two linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}1=A+B \\\\ 1=-2A-3B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we can write $A=1-B.$ Substituting this into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-2(1-B)-3B \\\\ 1 & =-2+2B-3B \\\\ 3 & =-B \\\\ B & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, find $A{:}$ \n\n$$\nA = 1-B = 1 - (-3) = 4.\n$$\n\n**Step 4: Write the particular solution.**\nSubstituting $A=4$ and $B=-3$ back into the general solution gives the unique solution to the IVP:\n\n$$\ny(x) = 4e^{-2x} - 3 e^{-3x}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152360 :activity/expected-seconds 1020.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
